1
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,120
(This story is entirely fictional)
Dad.

2
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:10,840
Xiao... Xiaoxue.

3
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,520
Run... run now!

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,520
Xiaoxue! Hurry...

5
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:13,440
Dad!

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,360
Let her go!

7
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:16,640
Dad!

8
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,080
Let her go!

9
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,280
Let her go!

10
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:24,800
Easy now.

11
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,120
I can point you to a way out.

12
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,440
(Based on novel Doctor Qin: Executer)
I've got a friend,

13
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,640
Mr. Zhang.

14
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:32,960
He's a charity donor.

15
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:35,400
He helps families in trouble like yours.

16
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,520
You could have your daughter

17
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,920
work for him for a while.

18
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,120
Good pay. Quick debt payoff.

19
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,160
See, I'm helping you out.

20
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:45,520
Don't hit my dad!

21
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:46,720
Don't hit my dad! I'll sign!

22
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,440
I'll sign!

23
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:48,440
Xiaoxue, don't sign!

24
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:49,600
I'll sign!

25
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:51,120
I'll sign.

26
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:51,760
Dad.

27
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,200
I can tell right away,

28
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:54,880
you've got more guts than your old man.

29
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:55,440
Let her go!

30
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,400
(Guarantor Signature)

31
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:07,900
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 14=

32
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:10,800
Is this the woman?

33
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,920
I really can't confirm that.

34
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:18,280
(Liang,)

35
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,600
(I've got another lead here.)

36
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,760
(Seven years ago,
Liu Sanhao was charged)

37
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:22,560
(with intentional injury.)

38
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,080
(The victim was a woman)

39
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,160
(named Su Qingchen.)

40
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:26,960
(She refused to drink
with guys at a hotpot place,)

41
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,560
(so Liu Sanhao's men beat her up.)

42
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:29,920
(She was beaten severely on the spot.)

43
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,400
(Spine broken. Paralyzed for life.)

44
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,760
(Later, Liu Sanhao got
a suspended sentence.)

45
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,760
Severely injured?
And he only got probation?

46
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:41,480
What's going on?

47
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,560
A victim.

48
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,400
Su Qingchen.

49
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,320
She might have a motive for revenge.

50
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,560
You stay here and keep investigating.

51
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,280
Got it.

52
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,280
(Serves him right!)

53
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:57,120
Serves him right!

54
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,440
(Karma Comes Around)
Who told you to make a scene here?

55
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:00,360
(Thug Liu Sanhao Got What He Deserved)
Be reasonable. Don't cause trouble!

56
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,440
Officers,

57
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,400
thank God justice has been done.

58
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:03,800
(Exactly.)

59
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:05,560
That menace is finally gone!

60
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:06,720
My daughter

61
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:08,440
has finally gotten justice!

62
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,160
Right?

63
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:09,840
Yes!

64
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:49,800
What are you doing here?

65
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:52,200
Just passing by.

66
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:54,680
What a coincidence.

67
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:06,960
Liu Sanhao is dead.

68
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:09,320
Liu Sanhao?

69
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,200
Su Qingchen's father brought people,

70
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,280
banging gongs and drums.

71
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,880
Lots of people gathered around,

72
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,320
saying Liu deserved to die.

73
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:19,000
Some people

74
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:20,960
just aren't worth mourning
when they die.

75
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,000
But if everyone in the world

76
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,320
cheers for a murder,

77
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,280
then what's the point

78
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,920
of us truth-seekers doing what we do?

79
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,560
Everyone's got their own position.

80
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,000
We're the same.

81
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,800
We're both doing what we think is right,

82
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,560
aren't we?

83
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,200
Get some rest.

84
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,280
That's a long way

85
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:44,320
to pass by.

86
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,480
Hello.

87
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,160
We're with
the Longfan Criminal Investigation Team.

88
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:03,560
Ms. Su,

89
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,360
we'd like to ask you a few things.

90
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,880
It's about Liu Sanhao.

91
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,120
What's in the file

92
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,080
might not be
the whole truth from back then.

93
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,320
We want to know

94
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,080
what really happened.

95
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,160
Ms. Su.

96
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:35,080
The truth?

97
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,560
You want to know

98
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:44,000
how I went
from a perfectly healthy person

99
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,280
to this wreck

100
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,320
with a urine bag hanging off me?

101
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,200
Is that it?

102
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,720
(Certified Public Accountant)
(On that day nine years ago,)

103
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,280
(I got my accounting certificate.)

104
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,400
(I put on my prettiest dress.)

105
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,720
(I thought my life was just beginning.)

106
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,040
(But some people)

107
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,520
(casually)

108
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,360
(chained the rest of my life)

109
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,400
(to this wheelchair.)

110
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,560
To the boss!

111
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,320
What's the fun
in a bunch of guys drinking?

112
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:25,720
What's wrong with you?

113
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:28,520
Congrats.

114
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,000
Thanks for the meal.

115
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,560
What are you doing?

116
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:38,760
Grab some.

117
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:40,040
Is it cooked?

118
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:40,880
Yeah.

119
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,920
Whoa.

120
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,800
Well, hello, ladies.

121
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:49,160
Drinking by yourselves is no fun.

122
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,680
My boss owns this place.

123
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,720
Come have a drink with him.

124
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,360
Let's go.

125
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:58,440
What are you doing?
We don't even know you.

126
00:05:58,840 --> 00:05:59,520
You go.

127
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:02,360
Feisty, huh?

128
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,480
Check, please!

129
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:07,520
Don't push your luck.

130
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,760
What are you doing? Stop it.

131
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:09,680
Let go of me!

132
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:12,640
Go.

133
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,440
Move!

134
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:15,240
Get lost!

135
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,080
Sorry about that.

136
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:20,160
Sit.

137
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:20,560
Sorry.

138
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,320
Have a seat.

139
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,480
Are you okay?

140
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:27,520
Sorry about that.

141
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,720
Let me apologize.

142
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:32,720
A toast to you.

143
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:33,960
We don't drink.

144
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,320
I'll drink for myself.

145
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:44,400
We don't mean anything by it.

146
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,960
Just come sit with my boss for a bit.

147
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,600
Let's be friends.

148
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:52,920
Min,

149
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,080
the cab's here. Let's go.

150
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,360
Is it that hard to have a drink?

151
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:57,560
What are you doing?

152
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,000
Keep this up, and we'll call the cops!

153
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,320
Calling the cops?

154
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,120
They said they're calling the cops?

155
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,560
Go ahead.

156
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:08,000
Call them!

157
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:11,880
Go on, grab it.

158
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,320
Grab your phone.

159
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,480
Call the cops!

160
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:18,680
Go ahead.

161
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:20,240
Here,

162
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,000
I am the law.

163
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,920
It'll burn you bad!

164
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,320
Ungrateful.

165
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,320
Qingchen!

166
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:50,520
You like taking sneak shots, huh?

167
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:59,520
Some drinks you gotta take.

168
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:02,360
Some hurts you gotta swallow!

169
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:11,120
Call the cops,

170
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,400
and you'll end up like her!

171
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:18,520
In the end,

172
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:22,920
Qiao Shengchan who crippled me
got nine years.

173
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:25,520
But the mastermind, Liu Sanhao,

174
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,760
only got probation
because he didn't lay a hand on me.

175
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:36,040
And that's how

176
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:37,960
the case closed.

177
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,080
Officers,

178
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:49,280
you think that was the end of it?

179
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,360
The day before Liu Sanhao died,

180
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:54,440
Chen Xiaolong...

181
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,520
Dad!

182
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:12,160
Then he asked if we were scheming
behind his back

183
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,440
and if we hired someone for revenge.

184
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,280
Look at my daughter.

185
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,680
What do we have to take revenge with?

186
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,720
He still wasn't satisfied.

187
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:25,440
(I knelt there.)

188
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:27,720
(I kowtowed to him.)

189
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:31,680
(I begged him to let my daughter go!)

190
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,640
(I begged him.)

191
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:47,440
Chen.

192
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:47,960
Dad.

193
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:51,640
Chen.

194
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:52,680
Dad.

195
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,520
Please don't get worked up.

196
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:00,880
Mr. Su.

197
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Listen to me.

198
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,360
The police

199
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:06,040
will give you an answer.

200
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,080
That's all for today.

201
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,200
Thanks for your cooperation.

202
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,680
Su Qingchen got such a raw deal.

203
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,440
Let's go.

204
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:47,120
Hurry back and organize all the files.

205
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:07,980
(As you ordered, I told them all.)
(Opens the door.)

206
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:40,060
(Get treatment. Live well.)

207
00:12:05,780 --> 00:12:07,470
(How evil can one person be?
Even toward his own kind,)

208
00:12:07,470 --> 00:12:09,180
(he can ruthlessly bite through
their body and suck their blood?)

209
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,400
How did your investigation go yesterday?

210
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:29,080
Qiao Shengchan, code name Heipi.

211
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:32,040
Liu Sanhao's number one enforcer.

212
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:34,400
He's the one who attacked Su Qingchen.

213
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:36,680
How's yours going?

214
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,760
In Su Qingchen's case,

215
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:40,080
Qiao Shengchan was sentenced
to nine years.

216
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:43,080
The file says he actively
rehabilitated himself in prison

217
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:45,280
and was named
a model inmate multiple times.

218
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:48,400
Five months ago, he got a reduced
sentence and was released early.

219
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,280
Now his registered residence
and actual whereabouts don't match.

220
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:52,280
After release,

221
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:56,200
he didn't report
to the local police station,

222
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:58,840
and there's no record of where he stayed
or any phone calls.

223
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,680
It's been five months.

224
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:01,840
He just vanished into thin air.

225
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:05,440
Mr. Dong.

226
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:06,840
No one in this world

227
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,880
just vanishes for no reason.

228
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,720
Find him even if you have to

229
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,840
turn Longfan upside down.

230
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:14,720
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

231
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,040
You two didn't sleep again, did you?

232
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,520
I'll have the cafeteria

233
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,440
add some extra nutrition to your meals.

234
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,400
Thanks, Mr. Dong.

235
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:28,060
(Qiao Shengchan
Inmate Intake Form)

236
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:31,920
No family came to pick him up
when he got out.

237
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,280
The emergency contact he listed
was Liu Sanhao.

238
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,680
But the number's already disconnected.

239
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:37,680
Disconnected?

240
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:39,560
We checked the car too.

241
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:40,680
(Longfan No. 1 Prison)
It's a cloned-plate car.

242
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:41,680
No way to trace it.

243
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:54,100
(No. 26 Dongqiaotou)

244
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:00,320
No. 26 Dongqiaotou.

245
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,640
This is the place.

246
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,080
Who are you two looking for?

247
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,080
Ma'am,

248
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,280
we're with
the Longfan Criminal Investigation Team.

249
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:12,040
We'd like to ask you something.

250
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,000
Is this Qiao Shengchan's home?

251
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,440
You're looking for the Qiao family?

252
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,800
Nobody's there anymore.

253
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,040
His mother passed away last year.

254
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,000
What about his wife?

255
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,560
She moved away a long time ago.

256
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:22,520
Heard someone took her to the city
to live the good life.

257
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:23,720
Never came back.

258
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:24,560
Thanks.

259
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:25,200
No problem.

260
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:36,760
Hello.

261
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:38,720
Hello.

262
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:41,440
We're with
the Longfan Criminal Investigation Team.

263
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,000
We'd like to ask you a few things.

264
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,880
Qiao Shengchan got out of prison
five months ago.

265
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:46,920
Has he been back?

266
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,280
You know Liu Sanhao, right?

267
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:54,520
Has he met with you?

268
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,520
Did he warn you

269
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,800
not to see Qiao Shengchan?

270
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,400
(Eight Years Ago)
Hey,

271
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:24,880
don't just sit there.

272
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,080
Eat up.

273
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:30,400
Look, I prepared all this just for you.

274
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,120
Look how thin

275
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,280
you've gotten.

276
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:36,760
Thanks, Hao.

277
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:37,880
I'll help myself.

278
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:40,760
Don't be so formal with me.

279
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,360
Shengchan worries about you
and his mother the most

280
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,560
while he's inside.

281
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:49,280
From now on,

282
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,520
if you ever have trouble,

283
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,280
like you're short on money

284
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:56,560
or feeling lonely,

285
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:57,880
just come to me.

286
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:58,600
Thanks.

287
00:15:58,600 --> 00:15:59,600
My mother-in-law's home alone.

288
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,520
I need to get back.

289
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:02,240
Don't rush off.

290
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,280
You haven't even eaten or had a drink.

291
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:07,160
That's real disrespectful.

292
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,320
Come on, sit down.

293
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:13,680
Sit down and talk with me.

294
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,480
Let's talk about Shengchan.

295
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,160
Hands to yourself.

296
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:20,280
Let go of me!

297
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,480
I just wanna take good care of you

298
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:24,600
for my buddy.

299
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,520
He's still got years to serve in there.

300
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,680
Must be rough

301
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,480
being all alone.

302
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,360
Let go of me!

303
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,240
Let me go!

304
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:03,180
(Longfan No. 1 Prison)

305
00:17:14,430 --> 00:17:18,570
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

306
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:23,230
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

307
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:27,560
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

308
00:17:28,050 --> 00:17:31,890
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

309
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:44,780
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

310
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:47,700
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

311
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:51,900
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

312
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:56,130
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

313
00:17:56,130 --> 00:18:00,860
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

314
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:05,100
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

315
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:09,620
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

316
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:13,910
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

317
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:26,900
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

318
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:31,240
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

319
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:35,030
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

320
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:37,930
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

321
00:18:37,930 --> 00:18:42,710
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

322
00:18:42,710 --> 00:18:47,430
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

323
00:18:47,430 --> 00:18:49,670
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

324
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,730
♪We stop here in this night♪

325
00:18:51,730 --> 00:18:56,180
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

326
00:18:56,180 --> 00:19:02,190
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

327
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:11,110
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

